<task id="036" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-20 — flag-gated swap: systemuser root sets from Dataverse's answer; keep the contact-grants union; canary-gated merge</title>
    <phase>1 One evaluator</phase>
    <gate>after-032-034-035; MERGE GATED on task 034 canary green (NFR-04)</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs change on the row-level-security boundary; tags bff-api/auth.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>FR-20 fail-OPEN risk (orchestrator directive): this is the task where an inert impersonation header becomes an org-wide disclosure — highest blast radius in the phase.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies AccessibleRecordSetService.cs (orchestrator hot-file list) + ExternalAccessModule.cs.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>032, 034, 035, 104, 142, 143</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days (was 3-4 hours; scope extended 2026-09-30 by the owner C9 rule)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Swap the SOURCE of systemuser root sets inside AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeForSystemUserAsync from MembershipResolverService pattern-matching to ImpersonatedRootSetSource (task 035), behind a config flag whose DEFAULT is the existing membership path (fail-safe rollout). KEEP THE CONTACT-GRANTS UNION unchanged — grants live in sprk_externalrecordaccess, not POA; Dataverse cannot see them (register B-17). Surface truncation honestly per NFR-03. This task's PR MUST NOT merge until the task-034 negative canary is green in the gate — equality between impersonated and app-only row counts means impersonation is inert.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET authorization internals + feature-flag rollout discipline. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>(SCOPE EXTENDED 2026-09-30: the SECOND amendments block at the end of this file binds on top of this goal. Per-record rights come from Dataverse, never the MembershipTermRights constant; owningbusinessunit stops conferring; the flag is not enabled until 142 and 143 are complete. Where this goal says "at the rights level task 032 assigned", read "at the per-record rights Dataverse returns".) ComposeForSystemUserAsync consults ImpersonatedRootSetSource when ExternalAccess:ImpersonatedRootSets:Enabled = true (default false), contributing the Dataverse-answer term at the rights level task 032 assigned to the systemuser plane; contact-grants union preserved verbatim on both flag states; AccessibleRecordSet carries a Truncated flag surfaced on the module data response; runbook records the prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser prerequisite.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §4.4: Dataverse applies ownership, role depth, BU, teams, POA shares, hierarchy — both pattern-matching defects (BU over-grant, POA under-grant) disappear. Investigation 08 §4: everything downstream consumes only the id set/rights map, so the swap is contained in ComposeForSystemUserAsync; watch items — keep the contact-grants union (§4-2), copy CommunicationThreadReadService's no-app-only-fallback refusal (§3a-2), decide truncation semantics for broad-role users whose REAL set can vastly exceed 5000 where pattern-matching structurally could not (§2). NFR-03: caps must never be silent — "Only 5,000 records displayed".</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.template.json (⚠️ there is NO appsettings.json in this repo — verified at HEAD 2026-09-21. The five files that exist are appsettings.template.json, appsettings.Testing.json, appsettings.Development.json.template, appsettings.Production.json.template and appsettings.tokens.md. The template already carries an "ExternalAccess" section at :66 and documents it with the "_ExternalAccess_comment" sibling-key convention at :65 — extend that section, do not create a new file.)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs</file>
