    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="032" status="completed">Rights-map evaluator (the Dataverse-answer term contributes into the additive max).</dependency>
      <dependency task="034" status="blocked-shipped">NFR-04 negative canary — BLOCKING MERGE GATE for this PR; cite the green run in the PR description.</dependency>
      <dependency task="035" status="completed">ImpersonatedRootSetSource (the new source being swapped in).</dependency>
      <dependency task="104" status="completed">Added 2026-09-15 (register ISS-013 / #990): the shared impersonation helper must fail closed before this task turns impersonated root sets on — otherwise a call site that bypasses RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync silently runs an app-only, unscoped query. Re-derive the status from 104's own POML (these attributes drift).</dependency>
      <dependency task="142" status="pending">Added 2026-09-30 (owner C9 rule, amendments block below). "Assigned To *" access for internal users must first be materialized as Dataverse shares. Once this swap omits the BFF membership term for systemusers, a Dataverse share is the only way that access survives.</dependency>
      <dependency task="143" status="pending">Added 2026-09-30 (owner C9 rule plus Q4). The No Access List must first apply to internal users on secure records in Dataverse terms, so the internal half of the No Access feature is not lost when Dataverse becomes the decider for systemusers.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-04">Scope: merge of this task. The negative canary MUST be green before merge; equality (impersonation inert) fails the build. The PR description MUST link the canary run. Merging without it is forbidden regardless of unit-test state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="register B-17 / spec FR-20">Scope: ComposeForSystemUserAsync. The contact-grants union term MUST survive on BOTH flag states — deleting or gating it removes access Dataverse knows nothing about. A regression test pins it under flag-on.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">Scope: the flag design. Default = false (existing membership path). Flag evaluation happens once per composition, is logged with the active source, and flag-off requires zero configuration (Null-Object/absent-config semantics — the kill-switch direction is BACK to the proven path).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-01 + investigation 08 §3a-2">Scope: failure handling under flag-on. If the impersonated source throws (including Guid.Empty from a principal missing SystemUserId), the composition FAILS (deny) — MUST NOT fall back to the membership path or an app-only query mid-request, because a silent fallback reintroduces the over-grant the flag was supposed to remove.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-03">Scope: truncation. When the impersonated set hits its cap, AccessibleRecordSet carries Truncated=true and the external module data response exposes it so the client can render "Only 5,000 records displayed". Silent truncation is a defect.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR (BFF-touching). State the placement decision citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md; run dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/ and report compressed size + diff vs ~44.96 MB baseline; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-10">🔴 THE NFR-04 CANARY IS NOW A **MANUAL** PRE-MERGE GATE — RUN IT BY HAND BEFORE THIS TASK MERGES. The owner decided 2026-09-10 that the live Dataverse assertions will NOT run in CI ("we do not need to have this dataverse test; this seems like overkill and introduce too much complexity to the CI"). That decision is accepted, and it makes THIS task the single place the check cannot be skipped, because TASK-INDEX calls 034 "a blocking merge gate for 036". WHAT TO RUN: task 034's NFR-04 canary against dev — compare the impersonated root-set read against the app-only read for the same user. PASS = the impersonated set is STRICTLY SMALLER. 🔴 EQUALITY IS A FAILURE, NOT A PASS: equal sets mean impersonation is INERT and the query is silently returning org-wide rows — a disclosure that looks exactly like success, which is the entire reason NFR-04 exists. Do NOT flip the flag on an equality result; STOP and escalate. ⚠️ ALSO NOTE: until 2026-09-09 this gate was GUARANTEED to lie, because every root-BU user inherited System Administrator via the BU's default owner team, so both reads returned everything and would have compared equal — a confident false pass. The owner removed that role and the main session verified it (root BU default team roles=[], and the previously-exposed user now gets 403), but THE CANARY HAS NOT BEEN RE-MEASURED SINCE. So this is a first real measurement, not a re-confirmation: do not assume the fix restored a meaningful inequality. Record the two set sizes in notes/ so the next person can see what "strictly smaller" actually meant here. Rationale: spec.md § "No Dataverse credential in CI".</constraint>
  </constraints>

