    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Verify tasks 032/035 merged and task 034's canary is green in the gate. Read ComposeForSystemUserAsync as it stands post-032.</step>
    <step order="1">Add the ExternalAccess:ImpersonatedRootSets:Enabled option (default false) with an options class; document both states under the existing "ExternalAccess" section of appsettings.template.json, using the file's "_ExternalAccess_comment" sibling-key convention (JSON has no comment syntax — that convention is how this repo documents a setting).</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the flag-on branch: root ids for the three root types from ImpersonatedRootSetSource; contribute as the Dataverse-answer term (design §4.5 term 1) into the additive max; membership term omitted on this plane under flag-on; contact-grants union untouched.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement failure handling per the NFR-01 constraint (throw → gate denies; log with the [WF-AUTHZ] prefix and the active source).</step>
    <step order="4">Propagate Truncated from the source onto AccessibleRecordSet and out through the external module data response; verify the field reaches the client payload.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: flag-off byte-equivalent behavior (existing suite green untouched); flag-on term-source assertions incl. shared-record-appears (POA fix direction) and BU-only-record-absent (over-grant fix direction) via substituted source; contact-grants union present under both states; source-throw → deny; truncation propagation.</step>
    <step order="6">Update docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md §6: prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser grant on the BFF application user + the warning that the app user must stay Org-scoped (impersonated privileges are the intersection — a narrow app user silently UNDER-grants; register E-2/E-3).</step>
    <step order="7">Build + tests; publish-size measurement per §10; PR description cites: canary run, ADR-028 A2 amendment (task 031), placement decision, flag rollout plan.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the task-034 canary is not green (or cannot run) at merge time, STOP — do not merge, do not downgrade the gate to a follow-up. Escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the canary state.</trigger>
    <trigger>If truncation semantics for broad-role users require a product decision beyond the Truncated flag (e.g. top-N ordering choice when capping — open register item C-1), implement the cap + flag and escalate the ordering question rather than choosing silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Flag OFF (default): composition behavior is identical to pre-task state — full existing unit suite green with zero test edits for this branch.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Flag ON: a record SHARED with the caller (present in the impersonated answer, absent from membership) appears in the composed set (FR-20 acceptance, under-grant fixed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Flag ON negative: a record matched only by owningbusinessunit where the caller's role does not cover it (absent from the impersonated answer, present in membership pattern-matching) does NOT appear (FR-20 acceptance, over-grant fixed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Flag ON: a systemuser who is also a granted contact retains grant-derived ids — contact-grants union pinned by test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: impersonated-source throw (incl. missing SystemUserId) → composition fails → gate denies; NO fallback to membership or app-only, asserted by test.</criterion>
