  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-20/NFR-02/NFR-03/NFR-04; design §4.4; investigation 08 §4 + §6 T2/T5 (runbook half of T5 lands here; the uac-access-control.md drift fix belongs to the docs-drift workstream, not this task). The blanket Collaborate stamp was deleted in task 033 — verify it has not crept back (grep WorkforceProjectAccessLevel = 0 hits).</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>

  <amendments date="2026-09-30" source="analysis of spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1 task 062 after the master merge">
    <verdict>SCOPE UNCHANGED. word-add-in-r1 task 062 (merged to master 2026-09-30) did NOT do this task's work,
    did not duplicate its seam, and did not weaken its gate. It is a SIBLING consumer of the same primitive one
    layer below this task's swap point: 062 trims the Office add-in picker SEARCH (/api/office/search/entities)
    by calling IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery directly; this task swaps the source of the accessible-record SET
    in AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeForSystemUserAsync via IImpersonatedRootSetSource, which itself calls the
    same seam. Both terminate in DataverseWebApiService.RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync. None of this task's
    five obligations is discharged by 062 (flag + options class; the ComposeForSystemUserAsync swap; the
    contact-grants union; Truncated propagation per NFR-03; the live NFR-04 canary), and IImpersonatedRootSetSource
    still has ZERO consumers on master — registered-but-inert, exactly as task 035 left it. Do not close, narrow
    or rewrite the steps. (Note the number collision: THIS project also has a task 062, the NFR-05 role-depth
    assertion — unrelated.)</verdict>
    <amendment n="1">062 is a SECOND shipped consumer of the impersonated-read seam in a non-Communication domain
    (alongside the Communication read paths). That strengthens task 035's CLAUDE.md §11 reuse argument and the
    #966 interface-rename follow-up (IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery is now generic in all but name: three consumer
    families — Communication, the Office picker, ExternalAccess root sets).</amendment>
    <amendment n="2">For the NFR-01 no-app-only-fallback discipline, add a SECOND canonical reference alongside
    CommunicationThreadReadService: OfficeService's multi-query impersonated fan-out (the "all impersonated reads
    failed → throw, do not return empty" rule, rationale "an impersonation privilege that is not configured must
    not look like an empty tenant"). It is closer in shape to this task than the single-query communication path —
    a per-type fan-out with a partial-failure policy.</amendment>
    <amendment n="3">🔴 RAISES THE PRIORITY OF STEP 6. prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser is now a hard runtime dependency
    of a SHIPPED, user-visible route (the Word/Outlook add-in picker), not only of the Communication read path.
    062's own completion note records it was never verified live. A missing grant makes the picker fail (closed,
    not leaking). The live state will likely be discovered by the add-in before this task's canary runs — a small
    de-risking of the canary, not a substitute for it. Step 6's docs obligation (auth-deployment-setup.md §6)
    currently has ZERO hits for the privilege on master.</amendment>
  </amendments>

  <amendments date="2026-09-30" source="owner C9 rule, session 27 round 2 BINDING (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md; defect C9 in notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md)">
    <verdict>SCOPE EXTENDED. The owner rule on 2026-09-30 is that a systemuser's Teams/SPA access EQUALS their
    Dataverse access, for both the set of records AND the rights on each record ("if a systemuser has access
    in dataverse then they have access in Teams/SPA ... do the full fix however that needs to be done").
    Swapping only the SET source (the original goal) leaves the flat Read|Write|Create stamp. That is defect
    C9's second half, and it is now this task's work too. Two more dependencies (142, 143) are added so that
    no internal feature is lost when the BFF-side derived membership stops applying to systemusers. Nothing
    in this block narrows the original obligations (flag, contact-grants union, NFR-01 no-fallback, NFR-03
    Truncated, NFR-04 manual canary).</verdict>
    <amendment n="1" title="Per-record rights from Dataverse, not a constant">
    Under flag ON, each root id's rights on the systemuser plane come from Dataverse's answer for THAT caller
    and THAT record. Today every hit is stamped with MembershipTermRights = Read|Write|Create
    (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:288-289, applied
    at :1048-1051). The impersonated read in ImpersonatedRootSetSource proves Read only, so Write, Create,
    Append, AppendTo and Delete need a Dataverse rights answer. RetrievePrincipalAccess is the reference
    primitive. Reuse candidates, which must be considered BEFORE any new component (CLAUDE.md section 11):
    Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs (task 008: OBO, entity-set parameterised,
    fail-closed) and Spaarke.Core AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync
    (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:255, task 070). Choose between up-front
    batched RPA over the impersonated set and a Read map plus an RPA confirmation at the rights-gated route
    for the single record in hand. Record the round-trip count (NFR-02). Never re-introduce the constant
    for the systemuser Dataverse term.</amendment>
    <amendment n="2" title="SUPERSEDED 2026-09-30 by owner D1 — Dataverse's answer replaces the BU guess; nothing is removed flag-off">
    OWNER D1 (2026-09-30, binding): "a user with access in dataverse model driven app should have access to
    teams/SPA app". The earlier version of this amendment removed "owningbusinessunit" from
    PlatformOwnershipColumns in BOTH flag states. That would UNDER-grant flag-off every user whose Dataverse
    Read depth reaches the record through their BU/role (dev "Basic User" holds Deep Read on sprk_project),
    contradicting the owner's rule, so it is withdrawn.
    The rule now is:
    (1) FLAG ON (the end state): for the systemuser plane, Dataverse's own answer (impersonated root sets +
    per-record rights, amendment 1) IS the access. A user who reaches a record in MDA through ANY Dataverse
    path (ownership, team, BU/role depth, share) sees it in Teams/SPA with exactly the Dataverse rights; a
    user Dataverse does not admit does not see it. The BFF's membership pattern-matching (including the
    owningbusinessunit and owningteam terms and the MembershipTermRights constant) is NOT consulted for
    systemuser ACCESS. Nothing needs a grant to be visible.
    (2) FLAG OFF (transitional only): unchanged legacy behaviour. Do NOT edit PlatformOwnershipColumns and do
    NOT flip the MembershipResolverServiceTests BU pin; flag-off must never under-grant.
    (3) Rollout: the flag is the end state, not an option. Enable it in dev in the same rollout as this task
    once 034's manual canary, 142 and 143 permit; flag-off is transitional.
    The ADR-034 amendment (section 6.5 path B) is therefore REWORDED: not "owningbusinessunit stops
    conferring", but "for systemuser ACCESS on the SPA/Teams plane, Dataverse's answer replaces the
    membership rules; the membership walk remains for non-access scoping (briefing, AI scope) and for the
    contact plane".</amendment>
    <amendment n="3" title="New dependencies 142 and 143: no internal feature lost">
    Under flag ON, step 2 omits the membership term on the systemuser plane. Today that term is the only
    carrier of two owner-protected internal features:
    (a) "Assigned To *" access. Registry assignment columns naming the caller's linked contact confer
    access through the ADR-034 walk. The owner (C9, round 2 item 5) says "one of the core reasons for the
    UAC -- this needs to continue being a feature". Task 142 materializes it as Dataverse shares, so the
    Dataverse answer carries it.
    (b) The No Access List for internal users on secure records (owner Q4). Task 143 makes Dataverse, the
    decider for systemusers after this swap, honour it.
    The flag MUST NOT be enabled in any environment until 142 and 143 are complete. The deny-veto and
    Restricted pipeline (ApplyVetoPipeline, AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:357, invoked at :1090) stays in
    force on the systemuser plane on BOTH flag states; this task does not remove it. Note its fourth
    argument: today the call at :1090-1094 passes the MEMBERSHIP term (constant Read|Write|Create) as the
    set that survives the Restricted veto, and a Restricted record is re-stamped with that surviving value
    (:397-400). Under flag ON that argument MUST be the Dataverse term with its per-record rights. Otherwise
    the constant creeps back through the Restricted path while every other path looks correct. If 143's design makes
    the BFF-side deny veto on the Dataverse term disagree with Dataverse's answer for the same user and
    record, that is an escalation (below), never a silent choice.</amendment>
    <amendment n="4" title="Live facts that change the prerequisites">
    prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser is held in dev through the System Administrator role on the BFF application
    users "# mi-bff-api-dev", "SDAP-BFF-SPE-API" and "# Spaarke DMS-SPE Dev 1". This was verified by role on
    2026-09-30, not by a live call, and no Spaarke role holds it. Step 6's doc must state the actual source
    of the privilege (a role, not a direct grant) and that it is unproven live until the task-034 manual run.
    Task 034's two open decisions are resolved: the canary is a MANUAL gate, and it runs as an existing
    non-admin test user in the correct BU with no relocation. The NFR-04 constraint above stands unchanged.
    Equal sets are a failure.</amendment>
    <amendment n="5" title="Files added to scope by this block (relevant-files and outputs above predate it)">
    read only (NOT modified, per owner D1 — flag-off must not change): src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipResolverService.cs PlatformOwnershipColumns;
    do NOT flip tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipResolverServiceTests.cs BU pin (flag-off unchanged);
    modify: .claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md (A1.1) and docs/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md. The .claude/ file is
    inside the sub-agent write boundary (root CLAUDE.md section 3): if this task runs as a sub-agent, it drafts the text and the
    MAIN SESSION applies it.
    reuse (read first, extend before adding): src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs,
    src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs (GetCallerRecordAccessAsync :255).
    Any NEW rights-source type or interface needs the CLAUDE.md section 11 three-question justification (with grep evidence
    that CallerRecordAccessProbe and GetCallerRecordAccessAsync cannot be extended) in the PR before it is written.</amendment>
    <adr-tensions>
      <tension adr="ADR-034" rule="Amendment A1.1 makes owningbusinessunit an access-conferring platform ownership column (.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md:73)" path="B">Reworded per owner D1 (2026-09-30): for systemuser ACCESS on the SPA/Teams plane, Dataverse's own answer replaces the membership rules (so BU/role-depth access is honoured exactly as in MDA, and BU-ownership matching no longer over-grants); the membership walk stays for non-access scoping and the contact plane. Concise and full ADR-034 versions merge alongside this change. Path A rejected (the BU guess is wrong in general); path C rejected (no compliant shape makes a pattern match equal Dataverse's answer).</tension>
    </adr-tensions>
    <acceptance-criteria-amended>
      <criterion testable="true">Flag ON: a record the caller can Read but not Write in Dataverse composes to exactly Read. Write and Create are absent from its rights, and a rights-gated write route (for example external to-do create or document upload) on that record returns 403. Asserted by test with a substituted rights source.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Flag ON: a record where Dataverse grants the caller Write carries Write in the composed rights. Rights are never broader than the Dataverse answer for any record. Asserted by test.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Flag ON parity (owner D1): a record the caller reaches in Dataverse ONLY through BU/role depth (no ownership, team or share) APPEARS with exactly the Dataverse rights; a record matched only by owningbusinessunit that Dataverse does NOT admit does NOT appear. Flag OFF: PlatformOwnershipColumns and the MembershipResolverServiceTests BU pin are unchanged (no flag-off under-grant). Asserted by test.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Negative: a failed Dataverse rights lookup (RPA throw or non-2xx) denies the affected record or fails the composition. It never falls back to MembershipTermRights or any constant. Asserted by test.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Flag ON, Restricted root: a systemuser whose Dataverse rights on a Restricted record are Read only composes to exactly Read on it (the Restricted survivor set is the Dataverse term, not MembershipTermRights), and a contact-sourced grant on the same record is still removed. Asserted by test.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Flag ON, BU default owner team: a record owned by the caller's BU default team and absent from the substituted Dataverse answer does NOT appear (the owningteam route of the over-grant is closed flag-on). Asserted by test.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Negative (no constant left): with the flag ON, no code path assigns MembershipTermRights to a systemuser-plane record. A test fails if the constant is reintroduced for the Dataverse term (assert rights equal the substituted per-record answer across at least three records with three different rights sets).</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">The ADR-034 amendment (reworded per owner D1: Dataverse's answer replaces the membership rules for systemuser ACCESS on the SPA/Teams plane) — concise .claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md plus the full docs/adr version — is merged with or before this task's PR, and the PR cites it (section 6.5 path B).</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">The PR rollout plan names the date the flag is enabled in dev and states that flag-off is transitional (amendment 2); it does not claim the flag-off BU over-grant is closed.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, existing non-admin test user in the correct BU; flag ON; 142 and 143 complete and deployed): (i) the task-034 canary passes strictly fewer; (ii) for one record that user can Read but not Write in MDA, SPA/Teams lists it and refuses a write with 403; (iii) for one record owned in the user's BU (or by the BU default team) but outside their role depth, SPA/Teams does not list it; (iv) for one record where the user's linked contact is named in an "Assigned To *" field, SPA/Teams lists it through the Dataverse share task 142 created; (v) for one secure record with the user on its No Access List, both MDA and SPA/Teams deny it. Every observation, with the record ids, is recorded in notes.</criterion>
    </acceptance-criteria-amended>
